From 07e8ef7296f95adeb503e3a321953a3ed1a39719 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 17:02:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf: stop translating the proposal summary sentence via Lara
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Per feedback: the per-proposal Lara call for the "Created exclusively
for..." summary was both costing money on every single proposal AND
producing wrong results — the BRAND_INSTRUCTIONS given to Lara
explicitly say to preserve proper nouns/brand names, so capitalized
category names like "Aerial Escape"/"Wild Escape" embedded in the
sentence were being read as product names and left untranslated no
matter how many times a proposal was regenerated.

The sentence has a fixed English skeleton with a handful of dynamic
slots (guest count, dates, time-of-day, category names, mood names) —
none of which need per-proposal translation:

- buildProposalSummary.ts now takes a next-intl `t` + `locale` and
  composes the sentence from pieces translated ONCE: the template
  itself and the 4 time-of-day phrases (new proposal.summary.* keys in
  en.json, via site_copy — same mechanism as introTitles/
  closingParagraphs), the guest-count phrasing (reused from the
  existing proposal.hero.* keys), and the category/mood names (reused
  from configurator.experienceNames/moodNames — extracted the shared
  key maps into experienceMoodNameKeys.ts so the wizard and the summary
  builder don't duplicate them).
- Date formatting is now locale-aware via toLocaleDateString(locale),
  so "August" becomes "agosto" for free through Intl — no translation
  needed at all.
- sentenceBuilder() (joins the category/mood name lists) takes a
  locale and picks " and "/" e " instead of always "and" — a single
  common word, not worth a Lara round-trip.
- Deleted moodDescriptions.ts/experienceDescriptions.ts: dead code —
  their lowercase/snake_case keys never matched the actual Title Case
  values stored on leads.experiences/moods, so the lookup always fell
  through to the raw value anyway.
- Removed the per-proposal Lara call + Proposal.proposal_data.summary_it
  storage from /api/translate-proposal-experiences and page.tsx — no
  longer needed, the summary is correctly localized synchronously with
  zero Lara cost.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
